{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For from the top of the rocks I see him</b> — I see that they were created before the world was created, and the rocks." "<b>For from the top</b> — in gematria: הר המוריה (Mount Moriah). מראש צרים — in gematria: מזכות אבות (from the merit of the fathers)." "<b>From the hills</b> — in gematria: הן האמהות (these are the matriarchs)." "<b>Alone</b> — three times in the Masorah: עם לבדד ישכון, שכני לבדד in the twelfth [parashah] in רעה עמך בשבטך, כי אתה ה׳ לבדד — in the matter of the redemption that Balaam was prophesying concerning the redemption. For You, YHWH, alone, securely will You settle me — He was not angry all those days, therefore securely will You settle me." "<b>Shall dwell alone</b> — seven tagin on the shin of ישכון, to tell you that they shall dwell in the land of seven nations." "<b>Alone</b> — rises to the count of 40, to tell you that they shall dwell in the land of Israel, which is a journey of 40 days." "<b>לבדד ישכן</b> — rises to the count of 420, hinting at the days of the Second Temple." "<b>ל</b> בדד ישכן — in gematria: בימי משיח (in the days of the Messiah)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:59.415472050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}